  "claim_boundary": "A private campaign stage and runner now encode the exact protocol shape in one genie-app process. A keeper dialog retains one source-proven Registry-backed shared HTP engine while every logical request uses a newly created dialog and independent EngineState, then is freed. The plan binds one first short request plus five warm requests for each tier, exact prompt hashes, 2048 ceilings, per-request profiles and outputs, timeout monitoring, raw-first capture, and scoped cleanup. All stage hashes and permissions pass. This is host design/proof only: no campaign is authorized or executed, and no performance distribution or registry evidence exists.",
